    "intro_html":  "Kofta curry is Pakistani comfort food built on patience with an onion. You fry the onions until they are deep golden, whisk in yogurt instead of tomato, and drop hand rolled beef meatballs straight into the gravy to finish. The result is creamy without cream and rich without much money. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
